WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.250
Petén, in northern Guatemala, holds the
largest expanse of continuous rainforest

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.150
in Central America.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.030
Here lies a biosphere reserve, with
national parks that include Tikal.

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.930
Inside the reserve, rights to timber were
given to 12 community groups and 2 timber

5
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:17.770
companies.

6
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.010
So some villagers earn a living
by felling rainforest trees.

7
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.290
Can logging help save a forest?

8
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.570
Or is every tree cut just forest lost?

9
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:32.750
In this mission, you'll learn three tests
for whether managing a forest is sustainable.

10
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.910
Then you'll judge the reserve's
record: where it has worked,

11
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.130
and where it has failed.

12
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.270
Your mission: decide whether
logging can help save a rainforest.
